    "summary": "I built a seed-starting tray of four hex cells in a compact diamond at (0,0), (1,0), (0,1) and (1,−1). Each cell holds a half-depth drained bin (hex-bin-half-drain), which has drainage holes in its floor. I closed the open outer faces with 14 solid end caps and bolted the shared walls together with 5 joint bolts so the tray stays together. To show what it's for, I filled each bin with soil and planted a seedling: basil, butterhead lettuce, kale and sweet pepper. The configurator's check passed with no rule errors, no prop warnings and no parts colliding. The build has 22 parts and the estimate is about 1777 g of filament and 2594 minutes of printing. The configurator only checks how parts fit. It can't tell whether the printed bins will hold up to watering, damp or sunlight; that depends on the material you print in.",
